[{:db/id "q-108806/selection/a0235f8491fdffaa3d127a854137878c16eb82d37125646b0760b470bff01413" :answer/id #uuid "d7ea971f-84b0-52ee-a061-52b676f3e201" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(z+2)^{5}-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108806/selection/ae24b547e90410bc131ab821214e4a9e5e8af952f2dfecd82ce899bd6dbffe57" :answer/id #uuid "e1a72c85-fa92-5882-90ad-4f9e7ac46d1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(z-2)^{5}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108806/selection/07c5168f5f5da02aad8f04aedbe87dcff3d1bc169077b545049303ec47c916a3" :answer/id #uuid "6e660202-5d83-572f-8d4c-d92fee11baa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(z+2)^{5}-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108806/selection/c733f1f6c4f3ab643a8dce9fb17c2cf74d0b93cf1848681197ce411d76aa8e52" :answer/id #uuid "937f797c-f9e6-5347-b97e-1082ac3b700a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(z+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108806/selection/07fa79203543ec67bfc0e7c911d35c80a542b4842f8838c916e9fb0b0c2aa12d" :answer/id #uuid "a04aa864-9f87-5b4a-82db-5615de9b9bee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(z+2)^{5}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108806/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff2f6a15-42e3-5a01-a856-cd34e3fe1fab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108806/selection/07c5168f5f5da02aad8f04aedbe87dcff3d1bc169077b545049303ec47c916a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-108806/selection/a0235f8491fdffaa3d127a854137878c16eb82d37125646b0760b470bff01413" "q-108806/selection/ae24b547e90410bc131ab821214e4a9e5e8af952f2dfecd82ce899bd6dbffe57" "q-108806/selection/07c5168f5f5da02aad8f04aedbe87dcff3d1bc169077b545049303ec47c916a3" "q-108806/selection/c733f1f6c4f3ab643a8dce9fb17c2cf74d0b93cf1848681197ce411d76aa8e52" "q-108806/selection/07fa79203543ec67bfc0e7c911d35c80a542b4842f8838c916e9fb0b0c2aa12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108806" :question/id #uuid "53bd63e0-b7c8-588a-b02f-e455261c85c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-108806" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(5y-7x+2)^{5}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=5y-7x,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=5y-7x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-7\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{7}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{7}{5} & =(z+2)^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5(z+2)^{5}-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=5(z+2)^{5}-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108806/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29a290a2-bc9e-57bc-84f5-a21cba4848de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-107797"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+2y+5}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+2y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{2} & ={e}^{z+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{z+5}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2{e}^{z+5}+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802/selection/b1983284ad55aeb8f49848904951b01cc08f0b9a96613dd9761cb7ea418aaa62" :answer/id #uuid "8d336402-c00c-53ea-a816-7ea4fd82377b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+5\\operatorname{tan}⁡z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802/selection/6a1caf0ca7f2e01e34e754ff14b4a729d7c57208bf4f1e63177e70b9aa40b08b" :answer/id #uuid "1c9cd66f-e4bb-5662-abb7-6ace6be09272" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5-3{tan}^{2}⁡z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802/selection/09ac69a0e712f1f38a9e4c66d749ac77a661d1c790f5f355d50b68dfe64f77df" :answer/id #uuid "611d910a-f061-5d9b-8e02-dfab64887b98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{tan}^{2}⁡z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802/selection/5973c5d1f991c5f58ef5b0215d9908f5e621b9f94fc5d633edd6ae1d34868347" :answer/id #uuid "c7030cb8-72e5-5adb-992a-af6fe5d08de5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-{tan}^{2}⁡(z-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802/selection/573a308812de0513704f1af49657d5926f181f839244d538342031eac630458d" :answer/id #uuid "869ccc6c-69d1-5f0b-8761-4d264cf47322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79e07e1d-12ba-5797-b106-4412c6ccd42a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108802/selection/573a308812de0513704f1af49657d5926f181f839244d538342031eac630458d" :answer-field/choices ["q-108802/selection/b1983284ad55aeb8f49848904951b01cc08f0b9a96613dd9761cb7ea418aaa62" "q-108802/selection/6a1caf0ca7f2e01e34e754ff14b4a729d7c57208bf4f1e63177e70b9aa40b08b" "q-108802/selection/09ac69a0e712f1f38a9e4c66d749ac77a661d1c790f5f355d50b68dfe64f77df" "q-108802/selection/5973c5d1f991c5f58ef5b0215d9908f5e621b9f94fc5d633edd6ae1d34868347" "q-108802/selection/573a308812de0513704f1af49657d5926f181f839244d538342031eac630458d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108802" :question/id #uuid "769fb03f-07ef-54c0-8e28-ab259b3c1d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-108802" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={tan}^{2}⁡(3x-5y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=3x-5y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=3x-5y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3-5\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={tan}^{2}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108802/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29a290a2-bc9e-57bc-84f5-a21cba4848de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800/selection/ca1ac702c0835adc4eba7a536fde69fbef172c5082858c2eea7635046121d235" :answer/id #uuid "0fb9646e-3136-5d4a-8060-63be7ea26403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800/selection/e90cb0f9d69351b1f0fefc15e7859c89ba084139aecb1238746df0af10cb74d7" :answer/id #uuid "ef32ba9f-bd30-54e4-b321-0263fc7e08eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-{cos}^{2}⁡z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800/selection/e956cd165d0ac7dfa884da658b983c58912b9851adf220f48e82e7bd0988a945" :answer/id #uuid "38971647-8caf-5c5b-a7d8-2045d02ffa26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800/selection/36328474e67d4aa22b598ed1e5ab9be7a4fcd92d0ad98f5b128bafbeee641fe1" :answer/id #uuid "02a0f214-a82f-5ad4-90a7-51deda39e430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡(2z+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800/selection/bd4531ee5a0da125fef341f6cde50c59ee035d670a6bded664da5094be288d49" :answer/id #uuid "285cd11a-8f32-5914-8bd4-901e35ae2c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{cos}^{2}⁡(2z)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15f66041-f44e-5006-9cb0-51f8c7140a45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108800/selection/ca1ac702c0835adc4eba7a536fde69fbef172c5082858c2eea7635046121d235" :answer-field/choices ["q-108800/selection/ca1ac702c0835adc4eba7a536fde69fbef172c5082858c2eea7635046121d235" "q-108800/selection/e90cb0f9d69351b1f0fefc15e7859c89ba084139aecb1238746df0af10cb74d7" "q-108800/selection/e956cd165d0ac7dfa884da658b983c58912b9851adf220f48e82e7bd0988a945" "q-108800/selection/36328474e67d4aa22b598ed1e5ab9be7a4fcd92d0ad98f5b128bafbeee641fe1" "q-108800/selection/bd4531ee5a0da125fef341f6cde50c59ee035d670a6bded664da5094be288d49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108800" :question/id #uuid "0cadc7d0-f55e-571e-8683-ef2ab01dbbf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-108800" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={cos}^{2}⁡(2x-y+1).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=2x-y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=2x-y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={cos}^{2}⁡(z+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=2-{cos}^{2}⁡(z+1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108800/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29a290a2-bc9e-57bc-84f5-a21cba4848de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821/selection/b6f24ad63c4d17eb00460e33f19a5d814fcfbd0c485e422dfe99f3c0c71ab7f4" :answer/id #uuid "1faa357a-6ac2-53aa-a0b8-96edb9191b3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821/selection/424bd79aa1c22ae1c6d6ec7f69406f6f2d5ff938e1da0d0b54cea1d5d363ae87" :answer/id #uuid "cdfbcec4-811a-5a3b-bc07-00be21eb9ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821/selection/7c9ac8dc471c42560d8b31f4e516b6d2ed7fb5f9e779f234f49c56aea5bc3b9c" :answer/id #uuid "eb9c8884-3f5d-52f0-9cf4-7bea005112a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{e}^{2}}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821/selection/efd84c3e8c2157a65f1eee51259d9d2a5f01aef2112f970f5c515aa85e78d6b8" :answer/id #uuid "38ba1b00-7ff6-5edf-84ac-157cd5f4c444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821/selection/2cd07e77db44b6255f92b997ec7193cea97fee2187124e2b1cd87c89c042b4f5" :answer/id #uuid "bcc3e64b-ca52-54b7-bfdb-e1992800a84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2880ddbf-996b-5b4d-b960-2ba3c5b73276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108821/selection/424bd79aa1c22ae1c6d6ec7f69406f6f2d5ff938e1da0d0b54cea1d5d363ae87" :answer-field/choices ["q-108821/selection/b6f24ad63c4d17eb00460e33f19a5d814fcfbd0c485e422dfe99f3c0c71ab7f4" "q-108821/selection/424bd79aa1c22ae1c6d6ec7f69406f6f2d5ff938e1da0d0b54cea1d5d363ae87" "q-108821/selection/7c9ac8dc471c42560d8b31f4e516b6d2ed7fb5f9e779f234f49c56aea5bc3b9c" "q-108821/selection/efd84c3e8c2157a65f1eee51259d9d2a5f01aef2112f970f5c515aa85e78d6b8" "q-108821/selection/2cd07e77db44b6255f92b997ec7193cea97fee2187124e2b1cd87c89c042b4f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108821" :question/id #uuid "a8b5df87-edf7-5da6-a482-ae2863c92ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-108821" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{(x+y)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108821/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "29a290a2-bc9e-57bc-84f5-a21cba4848de"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108821"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856/selection/201045c6e6aad1900fe2d929c47fb1a62e1d8e39288f20c7b5ad1d77a1efcc80" :answer/id #uuid "c7ecfb8f-7928-5f4c-a51a-914dddb78405" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x+y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856/selection/8b202226a6cddab320311782e9e9439e652024e2d81634c38d51ea4297b12326" :answer/id #uuid "482e5744-893e-5031-b3c6-9b32ce3c882f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856/selection/75924649e951a25a817418bbaad5fd1603b5d58bb4f874d0ae0538a7570fd32c" :answer/id #uuid "028cc4a9-9ebd-5997-8a43-b5ec7985c28b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{x+y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856/selection/2396de9ebb7595212cf6ddace4f34f6514e5351880132f2324369a24dd8f1cad" :answer/id #uuid "6be975f6-ee24-57cc-8589-ed289767e760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{x+y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856/selection/affd5843da3a7a1221dea8dd518f9c725f8cded4afc0afb90dfa8f7e7e12ff95" :answer/id #uuid "4f2812d5-d1c1-521b-8111-af3fb4a61791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2}{\\sqrt{x+y}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0cc3624-9c91-5273-9673-260ede7d1559" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108856/selection/2396de9ebb7595212cf6ddace4f34f6514e5351880132f2324369a24dd8f1cad" :answer-field/choices ["q-108856/selection/201045c6e6aad1900fe2d929c47fb1a62e1d8e39288f20c7b5ad1d77a1efcc80" "q-108856/selection/8b202226a6cddab320311782e9e9439e652024e2d81634c38d51ea4297b12326" "q-108856/selection/75924649e951a25a817418bbaad5fd1603b5d58bb4f874d0ae0538a7570fd32c" "q-108856/selection/2396de9ebb7595212cf6ddace4f34f6514e5351880132f2324369a24dd8f1cad" "q-108856/selection/affd5843da3a7a1221dea8dd518f9c725f8cded4afc0afb90dfa8f7e7e12ff95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108856" :question/id #uuid "4f2db63f-c6f6-53bb-b50f-fb394fae795a" :question/math-academy-id "q-108856" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+y}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)}-1.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\frac{x}{2}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{z} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}} & \\,⟹\\,v=2\\sqrt{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-2\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-4\\sqrt{z} & =x+K \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-2) & =x+K \\\\ \\sqrt{z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-2) & =\\frac{x}{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{K}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2) & =\\frac{x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=\\sqrt{x+y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108856/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a35df900-489d-5f8e-9d9e-075352035790"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108856"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-107814"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{y+3x+2}-3.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=y+3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3 & =\\sqrt{z+2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{z+2}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z+2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int (z+2)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2(z+2)^{1/2} & =x+C \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z+2} & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{y+3x+2} & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=2\\sqrt{y+3x+2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721/selection/962d04938a2a2dd4b08dbdda7d99f5189a79dbcefff5c826fe02020a5db5bd01" :answer/id #uuid "1dd34ff0-33ef-511a-bf9b-7dbc7bc1303f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721/selection/87472ac3deb460c5e88814e88b475a59deed243d2e80a8cf3e98c33be226794c" :answer/id #uuid "2890a8da-e979-5809-a868-1392bdce9f26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{y-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721/selection/6ab2ed77583fe2a535f2ed1e6db2120b809f6e628a744adb6e29b662075b4f83" :answer/id #uuid "394b669e-28a7-5ceb-a0a1-895ef0c4e9da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{3x-y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721/selection/3834a174f79250a9ac1156d96ba9a76996e0cd99aa6f47605c9adc1dffc5d940" :answer/id #uuid "ee87797c-f636-5cdf-b2dc-da8ae75b2ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{3x-y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721/selection/3937876cdc8e1aa1b266d13b58efab86d7b1940910189351411952ad59a3d7df" :answer/id #uuid "9e081cb1-bc06-564a-bd68-73f488b1a2af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3x-y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "97c3f21d-3d69-5152-b1af-5a1b985b60b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149721/selection/3937876cdc8e1aa1b266d13b58efab86d7b1940910189351411952ad59a3d7df" :answer-field/choices ["q-149721/selection/962d04938a2a2dd4b08dbdda7d99f5189a79dbcefff5c826fe02020a5db5bd01" "q-149721/selection/87472ac3deb460c5e88814e88b475a59deed243d2e80a8cf3e98c33be226794c" "q-149721/selection/6ab2ed77583fe2a535f2ed1e6db2120b809f6e628a744adb6e29b662075b4f83" "q-149721/selection/3834a174f79250a9ac1156d96ba9a76996e0cd99aa6f47605c9adc1dffc5d940" "q-149721/selection/3937876cdc8e1aa1b266d13b58efab86d7b1940910189351411952ad59a3d7df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149721" :question/id #uuid "d67c5ca6-2de3-51e3-818f-bb3a4104e2f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-149721" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3-{e}^{y-3x}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=y-3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3 & =3-{e}^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-z}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int {e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{-z} & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n{e}^{3x-y}=x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={e}^{3x-y}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149721/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a35df900-489d-5f8e-9d9e-075352035790"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149721"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855/selection/dbe16452bf8b11c66cba6eb40e5f911bacd2ff73410852340c8b8eb21a7dfee0" :answer/id #uuid "447036c9-9619-5da1-af16-961df9abdaea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}{x-2y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855/selection/4a4c43cb44eca6026b4b4ddfb6f3799a1654ab490a1911a677eb67b6ea16b36e" :answer/id #uuid "edaea162-9751-5441-93a6-f8eab2a98b57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1}{x-2y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855/selection/884b24fa7482009eb64b3026bc3f0b6e9cc99e6c18ea9f6b787798a3098d038e" :answer/id #uuid "4cd07fa4-645f-5ad9-8d88-af788fbf21df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855/selection/b61302d10cede9111533707d36ac47234e9f291dbb3e79e58a9c948abd7d8956" :answer/id #uuid "4bf8b0f2-1fe1-5f9e-856e-a506df1d9d52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)-2}{x-2y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855/selection/09b9eea983d4680e67c464f55924f144e6408c5b3d5d9c40f0c0174666be5385" :answer/id #uuid "048b5deb-13d0-5721-b07f-ff26355736dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "704ada25-3bfc-54cd-8f9e-e98a1a38a966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108855/selection/4a4c43cb44eca6026b4b4ddfb6f3799a1654ab490a1911a677eb67b6ea16b36e" :answer-field/choices ["q-108855/selection/dbe16452bf8b11c66cba6eb40e5f911bacd2ff73410852340c8b8eb21a7dfee0" "q-108855/selection/4a4c43cb44eca6026b4b4ddfb6f3799a1654ab490a1911a677eb67b6ea16b36e" "q-108855/selection/884b24fa7482009eb64b3026bc3f0b6e9cc99e6c18ea9f6b787798a3098d038e" "q-108855/selection/b61302d10cede9111533707d36ac47234e9f291dbb3e79e58a9c948abd7d8956" "q-108855/selection/09b9eea983d4680e67c464f55924f144e6408c5b3d5d9c40f0c0174666be5385"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108855" :question/id #uuid "ec7f57b2-2ef2-56bc-99a6-43d73009fa00" :question/math-academy-id "q-108855" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{(x-2y)^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x-2y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1-2\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{z}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{z} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}} & \\,⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{z}+\\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z}{z}-\\frac{1}{z} & =x+C \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1}{z} & =x+K \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1}{z} & =C-x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1}{x-2y}=C-x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2y)+1}{x-2y}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108855/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a35df900-489d-5f8e-9d9e-075352035790"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858/selection/c463001717cc3d262ff753312258a54054505fc2ffca4e11298279392d87a662" :answer/id #uuid "718cd833-caf8-5b9b-8218-02131aad92a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{2x+y}(2x+y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858/selection/1dd372158e1c366086270b98545489efcf1c0bd836800f09a2035ef7bae3bd09" :answer/id #uuid "747df9ae-d37d-5857-89ae-e829fcbde98c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{2x+y}(2x+y)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858/selection/009a77b7a053c148b791f327f0b77051f69a38500ebae302b1b934fc8a19fad9" :answer/id #uuid "cb5b46df-4b82-5e94-99bf-e0d7213f7907" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{2x+y}}{2x+y+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858/selection/62717f8e102949621484e210b72fb8f3abb64f44401fa5e64180ac2a9230c50c" :answer/id #uuid "2b2ffbd7-b678-5004-a919-61ade09e054d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{2}^{2x+y}}{2x+y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858/selection/57fab4863cdbe49cb5cbb140e92591d7fd24d7f307fdbd20e451dd4c39d94336" :answer/id #uuid "f813ecaf-0a39-56ff-a3ef-950583546797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{2x+y}(2x+y-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8050a1-bba8-57c7-a54e-0ea1deee6644" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108858/selection/57fab4863cdbe49cb5cbb140e92591d7fd24d7f307fdbd20e451dd4c39d94336" :answer-field/choices ["q-108858/selection/c463001717cc3d262ff753312258a54054505fc2ffca4e11298279392d87a662" "q-108858/selection/1dd372158e1c366086270b98545489efcf1c0bd836800f09a2035ef7bae3bd09" "q-108858/selection/009a77b7a053c148b791f327f0b77051f69a38500ebae302b1b934fc8a19fad9" "q-108858/selection/62717f8e102949621484e210b72fb8f3abb64f44401fa5e64180ac2a9230c50c" "q-108858/selection/57fab4863cdbe49cb5cbb140e92591d7fd24d7f307fdbd20e451dd4c39d94336"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108858" :question/id #uuid "86b98f38-121b-564d-b2ca-dbad04433775" :question/math-academy-id "q-108858" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{(2x+y)\\,{2}^{2x+y}}-2.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=2x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2 & =\\frac{1}{z\\,{2}^{z}}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{z\\,{2}^{z}}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{2}^{z}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int z\\,{2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={2}^{z} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int z\\,{2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{z\\,{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{z\\,{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x+C \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(z-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x+K \\\\ {2}^{z}(z-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2x+y}(2x+y-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}) & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={2}^{2x+y}(2x+y-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108858/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a35df900-489d-5f8e-9d9e-075352035790"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9035"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\ln(x + y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z= x + y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z'(x) = f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x + y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 1 + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = \\ln z+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = \\ln z + 1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9037"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = x + y.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y) = x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 1 + \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = z+1.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|z+1| & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\ln{|x+y+1|}  = x + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y) = \\ln{|x+y+1|}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
